# Code owners. GitHub requests these people as reviewers automatically, and branch
# protection on main requires a code owner's approval before merging.
#
# Every area lists both people. A pull request author can't approve their own PR, so
# with one owner per directory, that owner's own PRs could never merge. With both listed,
# the other person is always the required reviewer. The first name is the area's owner;
# the second is its reviewer. Stream boundaries are enforced separately by the
# `boundaries` CI check (.github/scripts/check_boundaries.py).
#
# Later lines win. Stream A (core): @andrefongkc-cyber. Stream B (shell): @lucassnam.

# Default: shared files (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, CLAUDE.md, WORKPLAN.md, docs)
*                         @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam

# Stream A: core
/caliper/engine/          @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam
/bench/                   @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam
/tests/                   @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam
/docs/workplan/core.md    @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam

# Stream B: shell
/caliper/app/             @lucassnam @andrefongkc-cyber
/tests/app/               @lucassnam @andrefongkc-cyber
/docs/workplan/shell.md   @lucassnam @andrefongkc-cyber

# Joint: contract changes pause the other stream and need both people involved
/caliper/contracts/       @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam

# Repository settings and CI, including this file
/.github/                 @andrefongkc-cyber @lucassnam
